.TH NEWSCID 1 "October 2026" "NewScid 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
newscid \- Modern Chess Information Database and analysis workbench
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B newscid
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIFILE\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B NewScid
is a modern, high-performance chess information database and graphical analysis workbench designed as a pure Go and Vue 3 rewrite of Scid vs. PC.
It provides native reading and writing support for high-capacity SCID databases (.si4 index, .sg4 games, .sn4 namebase), multi-game PGN streams, and live UCI chess engine analysis.
.PP
NewScid introduces advanced modern features including multi-alias Player Personas with dedicated database synchronization, AI player simulation sparring bots, online account integration (Chess.com and Lichess.org), universal notation styling, a 16-NAG scorebook annotation palette, and spaced-repetition training modules.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Display command-line options and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Output version, git commit, build date, and runtime information, then exit.
.TP
.BR \-\-db " \fIPATH\fR"
Open the specified database (.si4 or .pgn) upon startup.
.SH MAJOR FEATURES
.SS 1. Native SCID Binary Database Engine
NewScid contains a ground-up Go implementation of the SCID database format. It supports reading and writing 47-byte index records (.si4), Huffman-compressed move streams (.sg4), and front-coded namebase tries (.sn4) with sub-second query performance across databases containing millions of games.
Database tools include physical compaction, custom multi-criteria sorting (Date, Elo, Event, ECO, Player), and signature-based duplicate detection.
.SS 2. Player Personas & Multi-Alias Consolidation
Unifies disparate database identifiers (e.g. FIDE OTB designator, Chess.com username, Lichess handle) under a single consolidated Persona profile.
Features include:
.IP \(bu 2
Automatic candidate suggestion matching names in the currently active database.
.IP \(bu 2
Consolidated career record and per-alias win/draw/loss breakdown statistics.
.IP \(bu 2
Dedicated autonomous .si4 database provisioning per persona with one-click extraction and deduplication of matching games from any opened database.
.SS 3. Online Account Synchronization & Blended Databases
Direct API integration with Chess.com and Lichess.org. Download and merge games directly into the active database, a dedicated persona archive, or a blended dual-mode repository with automatic signature deduplication.
.SS 4. AI Player Simulation Sparring Bot
Simulate and spar against any human opponent found in any database (or any unified Persona) at their calibrated playlevel.
The sparring bot extracts historical opening trees to play the opponent's true repertoire probabilistically, then calibrates Stockfish midgame skill (UCI_Elo / Skill Level) to match their historical rating.
.SS 5. Universal Notation Styles
Dynamically switches move notation across the entire interface without reloading:
.TP
.B SAN
Standard Algebraic Notation (e.g., Nf3, e4, Bxf7+).
.TP
.B FAN
Figurine Algebraic Notation using Unicode chess glyphs (e.g., ♘f3, e4, ♗xf7+).
.TP
.B LAN
Long Algebraic Notation with coordinate squares (e.g., Ng1-f3, e2-e4, Bf1xf7+).
.TP
.B Descriptive
Classical English Descriptive notation (e.g., N-KB3, P-K4, BxP+).
.TP
.B UCI
Universal Chess Interface engine coordinates (e.g., g1f3, e2e4, f1f7).
.TP
.B ICCF
Numeric telegraphic correspondence notation (e.g., 7163, 5254, 6167).
.SS 6. Tournament Scorebook & Annotation Palette
Full variation tree support with collapsible sub-variations, variation promotion to main line, and deletion. Includes a 16-NAG scorebook palette (!, ?, !!, ??, !?, ?!, =, ⩲, ⩱, ±, ∓, +-, -+, ∞, ⯹) and rich inline move comments.
.SS 7. Live UCI Engine Analysis & Multi-PV
Integrates with any UCI-compliant chess engine (such as Stockfish). Supports multi-PV candidate lines (1 to 5 lines simultaneously), interactive candidate line highlighting on the board, live evaluation graphs, and automated blunder detection.
.SS 8. Training Modules
Includes interactive Tactics Puzzle Trainer, Spaced-Repetition Opening Repertoire Builder, Progressive Tactics Challenge, and Database Puzzle Miner.
.SS 9. Tournament Crosstables & Standings
Calculates Round-Robin cross-table matrices, Swiss round-by-round pairings, Sonneborn-Berger, Buchholz, and Buchholz Cut 1 tiebreaks, and Tournament Performance Ratings (TPR) from any event in the database. Clicking any match cell immediately loads that encounter on the board. Supports ASCII text crosstable export to system clipboard.
.SH KEYBOARD SHORTCUTS
.TP
.B F1
Open Online Help and User Documentation.
.TP
.B F2
Toggle live UCI engine analysis.
.TP
.B F7
Open Tournament Crosstables & Standings dialog.
.TP
.B Ctrl+O
Open database dialog.
.TP
.B Ctrl+N
Start a new game.
.TP
.B Ctrl+S
Save current game into database.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Del
Mark or delete current game.
.TP
.B Ctrl+B
Open Setup Board / FEN Editor.
.TP
.B Ctrl+M
Open Database Maintenance & Compaction dialog.
.TP
.B Ctrl+H
Open Header / General Search dialog.
.TP
.B Ctrl+I
Import PGN game from text or file.
.TP
.B Ctrl+E
Export current game to PGN format.
.TP
.B Ctrl+C / Ctrl+V
Copy / Paste FEN position to or from system clipboard.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Space
Toggle Trial Mode (board sandbox).
.TP
.B Ctrl+Z / Ctrl+Y
Undo / Redo board move.
.TP
.B F
Flip board orientation.
.TP
.B Space
Toggle autoplay / game replay.
.TP
.B Left / Right
Step backward / forward one half-move.
.TP
.B Home / End
Jump to starting position / final position of game.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Home / Ctrl+End
Jump to first / last game in database.
.TP
.B ?
Display Keyboard Shortcuts dialog.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/newscid/
User configuration directory.
.TP
.I ~/.config/newscid/personas.json
Saved multi-alias Player Personas and profile definitions.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/newscid/
Default directory for user persona databases (.si4) and training repertoires.
.TP
.I ~/.scidvspc/
Scid vs. PC legacy directory automatically scanned for databases, engine options, and piece sets.
.TP
.I /usr/share/scid/bases/
System-wide reference, tutorial, and tactics databases.
